New: SolverGMRES, SolverFGMRES, and SolverMPGMRES have now a second template
argument BasisVectorType for the vectors storing the orthonormal Arnoldi
basis, which defaults to the vector type used for the solution. This change
allows to store the basis in lower precision, e.g., with
SolverGMRES<LinearAlgebra::distributed::Vector<double>,
LinearAlgebra::distributed::Vector<float>>, which reduces the memory transfer
of the orthogonalization step, while the attainable accuracy is still
determined by the solution vector type. This approach is inspired by the
"compressed basis GMRES" by Aliaga et al. @cite Aliaga2022.
<br>
(Martin Kronbichler, 2026/11/23)
